{
  "name": "Myasthenia Gravis",
  "remarks": [
    "This module models Myasthenia Gravis (MG), an autoimmune neuromuscular disorder",
    "characterized by weakness and rapid fatigue of voluntary muscles.",
    "The condition is caused by antibodies that block acetylcholine receptors",
    "at the neuromuscular junction. Prevalence is 150-200 per million (15-20 per 100,000).",
    "",
    "2026-08 remediation:",
    "- Onset: the pre-fix module rolled a single flat 0.02% lifetime chance at the",
    "  age-15 Guard, which cannot reproduce MG's well-documented bimodal age/sex",
    "  distribution (early-onset, female-predominant vs late-onset, male-",
    "  predominant). Replaced with an annual incidence loop (MG_Annual_Check,",
    "  same re-enterable Delay+router idiom as pneumonia.json/CIDP.json), gated",
    "  by an And(Gender, Age-range) complex_transition: women 20-40, 3e-05/yr;",
    "  men 60-80, 5e-05/yr; nobody else rolls. Source: Carr AS, Cardwell CR,",
    "  McCarron PO, McConville J. 'A systematic review of population based",
    "  epidemiological studies in Myasthenia Gravis.' BMC Neurol. 2010;10:46 --",
    "  documents the bimodal peaks and reports incidence estimates in the",
    "  4.1-30/million/yr range; the two bands here sit at the upper end of that",
    "  range (30/million and 50/million respectively), consistent with the late-",
    "  onset, male-predominant rise in incidence documented in more recent",
    "  cohorts (Gilhus NE, Verschuuren JJ. 'Myasthenia gravis: subgroup",
    "  classification and therapeutic strategies for a heterogeneous disease.'",
    "  Lancet Neurol. 2015;14(10):1023-1036).",
    "- Long_Term_Outcome (the quarterly maintenance-follow-up loop): the pre-fix",
    "  split was 80% continue / 10% crisis / 10% refractory-exit, with Crisis at",
    "  15% mortality. Modelling the loop as a two-absorbing-state process (the",
    "  same arithmetic used to characterise the bug -- P(eventual refractory) =",
    "  a / (a + c*d), where a is the per-quarter refractory-exit probability and",
    "  c*d is the per-quarter crisis-death probability), the pre-fix numbers",
    "  (a=0.10, c*d=0.10*0.15=0.015) resolve to P(refractory) = 0.10/0.115 =",
    "  ~87% -- i.e. nearly every patient who does not die of crisis eventually",
    "  funnels into the refractory/rituximab arm, when only ~10-15% of real MG",
    "  patients become treatment-refractory. Retuned to continue 0.95985 /",
    "  crisis 0.04 / refractory-exit 0.00015 per quarter, with crisis mortality",
    "  (Crisis_Outcome) at 4.5% (Alshekhlee A, Miles JD, Katirji B, Preston DC,",
    "  Kaminski HJ. 'Myasthenic crisis: clinical features, mortality, complications,",
    "  and risk factors for prolonged intubation.' Neurology 2009;72(18):1548-1554",
    "  -- reports 4.47% in-hospital mortality for myasthenic crisis in a large US",
    "  cohort). That gives per-quarter crisis-death = 0.04*0.045 = 0.0018,",
    "  annualised mortality ~1-(1-0.0018)^4 = ~0.72%, and P(eventual refractory)",
    "  = 0.00015/(0.00015+0.0018) = ~7.7%, both matching the task targets",
    "  (annual mortality ~0.7%, refractory <=10%).",
    "- Crisis management previously had no acute treatment at all: Crisis_Encounter",
    "  recorded the ConditionOnset and closed with no intervention. Added",
    "  IVIG_Crisis_Treatment (RxNorm 42386, administered, HCPCS J1599 -- same",
    "  ingredient/mapping CIDP.json's IVIG_Therapy already uses), the standard",
    "  first-line acute stabilising therapy for myasthenic crisis alongside",
    "  plasma exchange.",
    "- Advanced_Treatment (rituximab) is now administration: true, not chronic:",
    "  true -- it is a clinician-administered infusion course, not a self-",
    "  administered chronic prescription. RxNorm 121191 already maps to HCPCS",
    "  J9312 in rxnorm_hcpcs_map.json (same code mantle_cell_lymphoma.json uses",
    "  for rituximab), so no new export row was needed.",
    "",
    "RxNorm note: the pre-fix module used bare ingredient RxCUIs for",
    "pyridostigmine/azathioprine/mycophenolate and its own remarks proposed",
    "SCD upgrades to verify later. Verifying those against RxNav",
    "(rxnav.nlm.nih.gov) found two of the three proposed RxCUIs were wrong:",
    "199985 is 'troglitazone 400 MG Oral Tablet' (an unrelated, withdrawn",
    "diabetes drug), not pyridostigmine, and 896733 does not resolve to any",
    "RxNorm concept. Corrected mappings, confirmed via RxNav on 2026-08-10:",
    "  Pyridostigmine  -> 903857 (pyridostigmine bromide 60 MG Oral Tablet, SCD)",
    "  Azathioprine    -> 197388 (azathioprine 50 MG Oral Tablet, SCD -- already",
    "                     used and mapped by CIDP.json's Second_Line_Treatment)",
    "  Mycophenolate   -> 200060 (mycophenolate mofetil 500 MG Oral Tablet, SCD)",
    "  Rituximab       -> 121191 (ingredient CUI; kept as-is -- see above)",
    "Prednisone (8640) and rituximab's own suggested SCD upgrade (1656698, also",
    "unresolvable in RxNav) were left as ingredient CUIs: prednisone is not in",
    "this task's scope and already resolves via medication_code_map.json, and",
    "rituximab is administered/J-coded rather than dispensed, so no SCD is",
    "needed for it."
  ],
  "gmf_version": 2,
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "MG_Annual_Check"
    },
    "MG_Annual_Check": {
      "type": "Delay",
      "remarks": [
        "Annual timer and router in one state (see pneumonia.json/CIDP.json for",
        "the same idiom). Bimodal incidence: women 20-40, 3e-05/yr; men 60-80,",
        "5e-05/yr; nobody else rolls -- see module remarks for sourcing.",
        "ComplexTransition.follow takes the first true branch, so the two bands",
        "are mutually exclusive by construction (checked independently, not",
        "cascaded), and everyone else falls through to the unconditioned",
        "default, which just re-enters this same state a year later."
      ],
      "range": {
        "low": 350,
        "high": 385,
        "unit": "days"
      },
      "complex_transition": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "And",
            "conditions": [
              {
                "condition_type": "Gender",
                "gender": "F"
              },
              {
                "condition_type": "Age",
                "operator": ">=",
                "quantity": 20,
                "unit": "years"
              },
              {
                "condition_type": "Age",
                "operator": "<",
                "quantity": 40,
                "unit": "years"
              }
            ]
          },
          "distributions": [
            {
              "distribution": 3e-05,
              "transition": "Develop_MG_Onset"
            },
            {
              "distribution": 0.99997,
              "transition": "MG_Annual_Check"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "condition": {
            "condition_type": "And",
            "conditions": [
              {
                "condition_type": "Gender",
                "gender": "M"
              },
              {
                "condition_type": "Age",
                "operator": ">=",
                "quantity": 60,
                "unit": "years"
              },
              {
                "condition_type": "Age",
                "operator": "<",
                "quantity": 80,
                "unit": "years"
              }
            ]
          },
          "distributions": [
            {
              "distribution": 5e-05,
              "transition": "Develop_MG_Onset"
            },
            {
              "distribution": 0.99995,
              "transition": "MG_Annual_Check"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "transition": "MG_Annual_Check"
        }
      ]
    },
