    "Long_Term_Outcome": {
      "type": "Simple",
      "remarks": [
        "Per-quarter outcomes for the ongoing maintenance-follow-up loop.",
        "Fix round 1: the round-0 crisis rate (0.04/quarter) was solved",
        "backwards from the mortality target rather than sourced, giving an",
        "annualised crisis incidence of 1-(1-0.04)^4 = ~15.3%/yr and ~8",
        "expected crises over a realistic multi-decade remaining lifespan --",
        "real myasthenic crisis incidence is ~2-3%/yr with a ~15-20%",
        "lifetime cumulative risk (Wendell LC, Levine JM, 'Myasthenic",
        "crisis,' Neurohospitalist. 2011;1(1):16-22).",
        "Retuned to crisis 0.006/quarter (~2.4%/yr, in range) and added a",
        "small non-crisis death path (MG_Death_Other) so the ~0.7%/yr total",
        "mortality target from round 0 still holds. Two-path arithmetic,",
        "both per quarter:",
        "  crisis-death   = crisis * Crisis_Outcome's death share",
        "                 = 0.006 * 0.045 = 0.00027",
        "  non-crisis     = 0.0015 (MG_Death_Other below)",
        "  combined       = 0.00027 + 0.0015 = 0.00177/quarter",
        "  annualised     = 1-(1-0.00177)^4 = ~0.706%, i.e. ~0.7%",
        "Refractory-exit (0.00015/quarter) is unchanged: the eventual-",
        "refractory-share arithmetic (a / (a + combined-death-per-quarter))",
        "moves only from 0.00015/0.0018=8.3% to 0.00015/0.00177=8.5%,",
        "still comfortably under the <=10% target."
      ],
      "distributed_transition": [
        {
          "distribution": 0.99235,
          "transition": "Follow_Up_3_Months"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.006,
          "transition": "Crisis_Encounter"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.00015,
          "transition": "Refractory_MG_Pathway"
        },
        {
          "distribution": 0.0015,
          "transition": "MG_Death_Other"
        }
      ]
    },
    "MG_Death_Other": {
      "type": "Death",
      "remarks": [
        "Small non-crisis mortality path added in fix round 1 -- see",
        "Long_Term_Outcome's remarks for the two-path arithmetic. No cause-",
        "of-death attribution (not referenced_by_attribute to the MG",
        "diagnosis): represents the excess comorbidity/frailty burden of",
        "living with MG (aspiration, respiratory decline, treatment",
        "complications) rather than a discrete myasthenic-crisis event,",
        "matching the same 'Death_Other' idiom CIDP.json uses for its own",
        "non-crisis mortality path."
      ],
      "direct_transition": "Terminal"
